[36m(TaskRunner pid=1724981)[0m Let's represent \(z\) in polar form. Since \(|z| = 4\), we can write \(z = 4e^{i\theta}\) where \(\theta\) is a real number. This means \(z = 4(\cos \theta + i \sin \theta)\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1724981)[0m 
