[36m(TaskRunner pid=1724981)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1724981)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1724981)[0m The real part of this expression is \(324\cos\theta - 468\sin\theta\). To maximize this, we need to maximize the expression \(324\cos\theta - 468\sin\theta\). The maximum value of \(a\cos\theta + b\sin\theta\) is \(\sqrt{a^2 + b^2}\). So, the maximum value of \(324\cos\theta - 468\sin\theta\) is \(\sqrt{324^2 + 468^2}\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1724981)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1724981)[0m Let's calculate this:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1724981)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1724981)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1724981)[0m \sqrt{324^2 + 468^2} = \sqrt{104976 + 219024} = \sqrt{324000} = 570
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1724981)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1724981)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1724981)[0m So, the largest possible real part of the expression is \(570\). Let's confirm this with Python code.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1724981)[0m ```python
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1724981)[0m import math
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1724981)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1724981)[0m # Coefficients
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1724981)[0m a = 324
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1724981)[0m b = -468
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1724981)[0m 
