[36m(TaskRunner pid=1724981)[0m To find the maximum value of \(324 \cos \theta - 432 \sin \theta\), we can use the fact that the maximum value of \(a \cos \theta + b \sin \theta\) is \(\sqrt{a^2 + b^2}\). Here, \(a = 324\) and \(b = -432\), so the maximum value is:
