[36m(TaskRunner pid=1724981)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1724981)[0m Let's represent \(z\) in its polar form. Since \(|z| = 4\), we can write \(z = 4e^{i\theta} = 4(\cos \theta + i \sin \theta)\). Then, \(\frac{1}{z} = \frac{1}{4}e^{-i\theta} = \frac{1}{4}(\cos \theta - i \sin \theta)\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1724981)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1724981)[0m Now, we substitute \(z = 4(\cos \theta + i \sin \theta)\) and \(\frac{1}{z} = \frac{1}{4}(\cos \theta - i \sin \theta)\) into the expression:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1724981)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1724981)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1724981)[0m (75 + 117i)z + \frac{96 + 144i}{z} = (75 + 117i)4(\cos \theta + i \sin \theta) + \frac{96 + 144i}{4}(\cos \theta - i \sin \theta)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1724981)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1724981)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1724981)[0m Simplifying the expression, we get:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1724981)[0m 
